                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ddccadd4-54b9-31fc-b04a-d41156cbf0ac",
                        "entry_id": "1ff3882c-8ad8-38ec-9b3b-a99aad2ea648",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An orchestral keyboard player; one who plays piano or harpsichord for an orchestra or ensemble."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d8730c8c-7868-4f10-b199-10e428b0f0d4",
                                "sense_id": "ddccadd4-54b9-31fc-b04a-d41156cbf0ac",
                                "text": "Ensemble performances were led by the organist or cembalist ; he sat at his instrument, played the “accompaniment,” and directed the performance—now by movements of his head, now perhaps by beating time with one hand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b28c6d85-b11f-42c9-8c40-7ea1f3d6564d",
                                "sense_id": "ddccadd4-54b9-31fc-b04a-d41156cbf0ac",
                                "text": "While the symphonies of Haydn and Mozart could conceivably be played fairly acceptably under the dual leadership of concertmaster and cembalist, the symphonies of Beethoven could not."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2c8baa8-8d46-4c09-bbb7-99bfd3951911",
                                "sense_id": "ddccadd4-54b9-31fc-b04a-d41156cbf0ac",
                                "text": "The position of cembalist was one of equal honor and responsibility."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7188ead1-da86-4a75-b79d-501bd198eaed",
                                "sense_id": "ddccadd4-54b9-31fc-b04a-d41156cbf0ac",
                                "text": "For instance, we read that Emanuel was “hired as first cembalist at a salary of three hundred thalers” and that he was: somewhat relieved when Christoph Nichelmann ... was appointed second cembalist in 1744, although this appointment was an occasion for Emanuel's embarrassment: Nichelmann was given a salary twice the size of his."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
